There are 4 aces in the deck. The probability that the first card is an ace is \(\frac{4}{52}\). After drawing one ace, 3 aces remain among the 51 remaining cards, so the probability that the second card is also an ace is \(\frac{3}{51}\). Therefore, the required probability is
\[
\frac{4}{52} \times \frac{3}{51}
= \frac{12}{2652}
= \frac{1}{221}.
\]
